{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.WeightedPermutationCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.WeightedPermutationCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.OrbitQuotientCount"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.weighted_character_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.weighted_character_two","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L137-L150","doc":"**The physical weight.** With the fibre `κ = Fin 2` carrying `K = diag(1, q²)` —\nthe weight the corpus's Schur–Weyl normalisation uses — the character is\n\n    ∏_{orbits O} (1 + q^{2|O|})\n\na product of one `q`-binomial per orbit, indexed by orbit size. At `q = 1` each factor\nis `2` and this is `2^{c(σ)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.weighted_permutation_character_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.weighted_permutation_character_one","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L124-L135","doc":"**The undeformed limit.** At `w ≡ 1` every orbit factor is `card κ`, and the\n`q`-deformed character collapses to `(card κ) ^ orbitCount σ` — the character proved in\n`OrbitQuotientCount`.\n\nThis is the check that the deformation is the RIGHT one: it is not a new object, it is\nthe same character with the orbit SIZES retained instead of discarded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.sum_orbitSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.sum_orbitSize","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L114-L121","doc":"**The orbits partition the slots.** Structural sanity: orbit sizes sum to `card α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.weighted_permutation_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.weighted_permutation_character","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L94-L109","doc":"**The `q`-deformed permutation character.** With a weight `w` on the fibre basis,\nthe weighted trace of `σ` permuting the factors of `V^{⊗α}` is a product of one factor\nper **orbit**, each factor a weight-sum raised to that orbit's size:\n\n    ∑_{f invariant} ∏ᵢ w (f i)  =  ∏_{orbits O} ∑_k w(k) ^ |O|\n\nAt `w ≡ 1` every factor is `card κ` and this collapses to `(card κ)^{orbitCount σ}` —\nthe `q = 1` character. The deformation lives entirely in the orbit SIZES, which the\nundeformed count discards. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.prod_weight_eq_prod_orbits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.prod_weight_eq_prod_orbits","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L79-L92","doc":"A weight assigned per tensor slot factors over the orbits: an invariant `f` is\nconstant on each orbit, so its slot-weights collect into one power per orbit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.invariantEquivOrbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.invariantEquivOrbit","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L68-L74","doc":"Invariant functions are exactly functions on the orbit set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitSize","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/WeightedPermutationCharacter.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The size of an orbit of `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}